# Without this, Git's autocrlf line-ending normalization would treat *.pdf as a text file and
# rewrite LF bytes to CRLF wherever they happen to occur in the binary content — silently
# corrupting the file (PDF's xref table depends on exact byte offsets). Mark every binary asset
# explicitly as binary so Git never diffs or converts it.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary

# Scripts that run on Linux (the EC2 instance, GitHub Actions' ubuntu-latest runners, Docker
# Linux containers) must keep LF endings regardless of this being a Windows dev machine —
# CRLF in a bash script's shebang or commands breaks it in ways that are easy to miss until
# it's actually running.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sh.tpl text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
